## Current reading level
- Listening comprehension is stronger than independent reading
- Parents usually read aloud; he is beginning to try reading himself
- Target difficulty: Oxford Reading Tree Stage / Level 6 (longer sentences, more dialogue, richer plot)
- Parent note: ORT LV6 is comfortable for him; do not oversimplify below this unless asked
- **2026-08-21:** listening is easy — vocab should be a **slight** step up (story words + short phrases), not another pass of obvious nouns. See `docs/lesson-01-03-review.md`
- Needs strong pronunciation support: prefer pre-generated AI voice audio for full lines/dialogue; delivery should match story emotion, not a flat read

## Teaching goals
- Move from listen-only to guided independent reading
- Every lesson must include: vocabulary preview, story, comprehension with instant feedback, sight-word practice, and a teacher/parent follow-up notes area
- Keep language warm, encouraging, and age-appropriate (no scary or violent content)

## Project workflow
